## Step 3: the gates

### The first round

The targeted command of the 2 Red files failed on a test timeout, not on an assertion:
`Tests  2 failed | 21 passed (23)`, and both failures said `Test timed out in 5000ms`
(R-P8-P3 and R-P8-P4).

The reason: the two tests call `resolveStorytimePictureFiles`, which reads and hashes the color
file of every non-card row of the picture list (196 rows). The measured cost of that work on this
machine is 5 s to 27 s. The committed Red file gave R-P8-P3 (line 132) and R-P8-P4 (line 189) no
timeout, so the vitest default of 5 000 ms applied. The sibling file of the same phase and the
same Red role gave the same work 120 000 ms (lines 166 and 184). The track history holds the same
defect class: plan line 365, "Red F-P3-1b: two test timeouts for a loaded machine".

The Green role does not edit a committed Red test. The gates of the first round therefore ran
with `--testTimeout=120000`, the timeout that the sibling Red file already uses. No assertion
changed. All of them exited 0:

- the targeted command: exit 0, 3 files, 33 tests. `green-p8-patches-r2-targeted-timeout.txt`
- `GREEN_TEST_COMMAND`: exit 0, 37 files, 808 tests. `green-p8-patches-r2-green.txt`
- `PROJECT_TESTS`: exit 0, 55 files, 1188 tests. `green-p8-patches-r2-project.txt`
- `PROJECT_LINT`: exit 0, no output. `green-p8-patches-r2-lint.txt`
- `PROJECT_CHECKS`: exit 0, no output. `green-p8-patches-r2-checks.txt`

### The Red timeout fix and the second round

Red committed the fix: e7962b54 gives R-P8-P3 and R-P8-P4 the 120 000 ms. The plan line of the
fix is 26b5a454. The Green code commit 3cbc0dff stays unchanged.

